\subsection{Character Animation}
\emph{UniRig}'s ability to predict spring bone parameters, trained on the VRoid and Rig-XL dataset, makes it particularly well-suited for creating animated characters. Our method can generate VRM-compatible models from simple mesh inputs, enabling users to easily export their creations to various animation platforms. This streamlines the process of creating and animating virtual characters. For example, users can leverage tools like Warudo \cite{tang2024warudo} to bring their rigged characters to life in a virtual environment, as demonstrated in Figure \ref{fig:warudo}. This capability is especially valuable for applications like VTubing, where realistic and expressive character motion is highly desirable. The smooth and natural movements generated by our spring bone simulation contribute to a more engaging and immersive VTubing experience.


