Given a set of obstacles $\mathcal{O}$ and a collection of thin edges $\mathcal{E}$, we partition the plane into distinct \textbf{regions}, which are the empty parts of the plane bounded by obstacles or thin edges. A visualization of regions is shown in Figure \ref{fig:region}.
\end{define}

