We can represent this partition as a planar graph $G = (V, E)$, where each vertex $v \in V$ corresponds to a region of the partition, and each thin edge $e \in E$ represents a shared boundary between adjacent regions. Namely, each edge $e \in E$ is weighted by the ``bottleneck width'' of the corresponding boundary~--- that is, the minimum distance between obstacles along that boundary. 

