\subsection{Research Goals}
We investigate the following research questions:
\vspace{-3mm}
\begin{itemize}
\addtolength\itemsep{-3mm}
\item Can behaviors of multi-agent systems be predicted from isolated LLM behaviors?
\item Do emergent system-level behaviors affect multi-agent system reasoning and answers?
\end{itemize}
\vspace{-3mm}
To address these research questions, we execute several studies using the MAEBE framework, evaluating and comparing performance on the GGB benchmark to investigate the decision-making process and resulting preferences of MAS compared to responses of isolated LLMs. We find that question framing significantly affects LLM moral reasoning, that single agent performance does not reliably predict MAS behavior, and we demonstrate the emergence of specific group dynamics like peer pressure as classified by LLM-as-a-Judge methods. 

