\section{Broader Impacts}

The paper proposes the novel Quality-Diversity Red-Teaming framework for discovering diverse vulnerabilities and enhancing the safety and responsibility of large language models against a diverse range of attacks. 
By systematically discovering vulnerabilities in a diverse set of goal-driven behaviors, the developers can implement more robust safeguards and fine-tuning before deployment. We believe that the QDRT framework is a powerful tool for a comprehensive understanding of how the large language models can fail, which is a critical step towards building trustworthy AI systems.




