Because NAPOLY+ scales resource utilization with the number of states and transitions, the pruned graphs result in tangible reductions in hardware overhead. Our tool outputs a hardware-compatible representation of the pruned graph, which is then compiled into configuration vectors used by the HLS-based implementation of NAPOLY+. This end-to-end workflow, from symbolic graph generation to hardware deployment and performance evaluation, highlights AutoSlim’s versatility and practical value in real-world FPGA-based pattern matching applications.

