$\{y,z\}\in D$.  Because $y\in Y_j\in C_h$ for some $h\leq h^*$ where $Y_j$ is unmarked, the pair $(Y_i,Y_j)$ is $x$-compatible.   
Then can use the same arguments as above. We have that $\varphi$ maps the points of $Y_i$ into $t$-dimensional affine subspace $L$ for $t=|Y_i|-1$ and the embedding of $(Y_i,\dist)$ into $\mathbb{R}^t$ is strong. We fix the corresponding realization $S$ of $(Y_i,\dist)$.  
