    For the grid graph the starting state was the ``row'' partition seen in Figure~\ref{fig:initialgrid}, and for Colorado the starting state was given by the 2018 congressional districting plan.

    We note that SpecReCom does not take into account vertex weights. Therefore, while the plans may appear to be suitable for political use, their district populations are not necessarily well-balanced. For example, the partitions of the grid graph and Colorado graph in Figure~\ref{fig:specrecomplans} have population deviations of approximately 0.15 and 0.33 (respectively), both of which are worse than the majority of plans seen to be generated by RevReCom (see section~\ref{sec:results}).

