    The first buckling mode of the CBVSY design is local and is shown in \cref{fig:dehomBuckling:4} with clear buckling of the microstructure. However, the BLF is only \SI{1}{\percent} lower than that estimated by the homogenized analysis. The third mode of the CBVSY design is a global mode, shown in \cref{fig:dehomBuckling:5} and has a BLF that is only \SI{5}{\percent} higher than the first mode. This means that the first modes are almost active at the same time, which aligns perfectly with the formulation of the multiscale buckling constraint. If global failure was desired, the local buckling constraint could be updated with a safety factor similar to the approach suggested in  \cite{Christensen2025}.


